Third-party material

This product bundles third-party material under its own licenses, listed below. The per-file
list (author, source, license) is in assets/ATTRIBUTION.md.

Inter (assets/fonts/Inter-*.ttf) — SIL Open Font License 1.1. See assets/fonts/OFL-Inter.txt.
Place names (crates/geo/data/places.bin) are derived from GeoNames (https://www.geonames.org/), used under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 licence (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/); they were converted to a
compact form (columns dropped, names normalised and capped). World coastlines (crates/geo/data/land.bin) come from
Natural Earth (https://www.naturalearthdata.com/), public domain.
Showcase photographs by Ansel Adams, Dorothea Lange and NASA (docs/images/) — public domain. See assets/ATTRIBUTION.md.

crates/raw/src/spectral_table.rs (lightcraft-raw) holds camera colour matrices derived from the
camera spectral sensitivities, training reflectances and model alias list of rawtoaces-data
(https://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/rawtoaces-data, v1.1.0), an Academy Software
Foundation project licensed under the Apache License 2.0, and from the CIE 1931 colour-matching
functions it ships (CIE, CC-BY-4.0). The matrices were fitted by the LightCraft contributors
(2026) with tools/spectral_camera_table.py. See assets/ATTRIBUTION.md.

crates/inpaint (lightcraft-inpaint) ports the inpainting (PatchMatch completion) and Poisson membrane
fill code of PhotoCraft (https://github.com/storytold/photocraft, crates/algo/src/inpaint.rs and
poisson.rs), Copyright the PhotoCraft contributors, licensed under the MIT License or the Apache
License 2.0, at your option. The port was modified by the LightCraft contributors (2026); each
ported file says so.

crates/raw/src/vc5.rs (lightcraft-raw) ports the VC-5 decoder of GoPro's GPR SDK
(https://github.com/gopro/gpr, source/lib/vc5_common and source/lib/vc5_decoder, including its codebook 17
table), Copyright 2018 GoPro Inc., licensed under the Apache License 2.0 or the MIT License, at your
option. The port was modified by the LightCraft contributors (2026): translated from C to Rust and
restructured; the file says so.

crates/segment (lightcraft-segment) ports the SAM 3 model code of Hugging Face Transformers
(https://github.com/huggingface/transformers, src/transformers/models/sam3 and sam3_tracker),
Copyright The HuggingFace Team and Meta Platforms, Inc., licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
The port was modified by the LightCraft contributors (2026): translated from Python/PyTorch to
Rust on candle and restructured; each ported file says so. Because of this, crates/segment is
licensed under the Apache License 2.0 only (LICENSE-APACHE), not under the MIT option.

The SAM 3 weights are not part of LightCraft and are never distributed with it. A user downloads
the facebook/sam3 checkpoint only when they choose to (in the app, or by hand), under Meta's SAM
License (https://github.com/facebookresearch/sam3/blob/main/LICENSE), a separate, non-OSI
licence. See docs/ai-masks.md.

crates/enhance (lightcraft-enhance) re-implements the SPAN super-resolution network (Swift
Parameter-free Attention Network, Cheng Wan et al., CVPR Workshops 2024;
https://github.com/hongyuanyu/SPAN, basicsr/archs/span_arch.py, Apache License 2.0) and follows
its neosr and spandrel ports (Apache-2.0 and MIT), in Rust on candle. crates/enhance is
therefore licensed under the Apache License 2.0 only (LICENSE-APACHE).

Super-resolution weights are not part of LightCraft and are never distributed with it. A user
downloads them only when they choose to. The first supported model is Nomos Uni SPAN
(https://huggingface.co/Phips/2xNomosUni_span_multijpg, by Philip Hofmann, "Phips"), licensed
CC-BY-4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/): LightCraft credits the author where it
offers the download and in the files it makes with it. See docs/ai-models.md.

crates/diffuse (lightcraft-diffuse), Generative Expand's diffusion models, puts Stable Diffusion's UNet
together from candle-transformers' blocks following its unet_2d.rs (https://github.com/huggingface/candle,
MIT OR Apache-2.0), with SDXL's added conditioning, and re-implements Kandinsky 2.2's decoder UNet, its MoVQ
autoencoder and the inpainting pipeline following diffusers (https://github.com/huggingface/diffusers,
Apache License 2.0, Copyright The HuggingFace Team), in Rust on candle. crates/diffuse is therefore licensed
under the Apache License 2.0 only (LICENSE-APACHE).

The diffusion weights are not part of LightCraft and are never distributed with it. A user downloads them
only when they choose to, from their authors' Hugging Face repositories, pinned by size and SHA-256:
Stable Diffusion 1.5 Inpainting (stable-diffusion-v1-5/stable-diffusion-inpainting, Robin Rombach and
Patrick Esser, Runway / CompVis / Stability AI) under the CreativeML OpenRAIL-M licence and SDXL 1.0
Inpainting 0.1 (diffusers/stable-diffusion-xl-1.0-inpainting-0.1) under the CreativeML Open RAIL++-M
licence, both non-OSI licences whose use-based restrictions the user accepts with the download; and
Kandinsky 2.2 (kandinsky-community/kandinsky-2-2-decoder-inpaint and -prior, Sber AI / AIRI) under the
Apache License 2.0. See docs/generative-expand.md.

Search by description runs the SigLIP 2 B/16 model (google/siglip2-base-patch16-224, Google, Apache License 2.0)
through candle (MIT OR Apache-2.0) and the tokenizers crate (Apache-2.0). The weights are not part of
LightCraft and are never distributed with it: a user downloads them only when they choose to, from Hugging Face or a
mirror they configure, pinned by size and SHA-256. See docs/search-people.md.

Reading the text in photos runs PP-OCRv6 small (PaddlePaddle/PP-OCRv6_small_det_onnx and _rec_onnx, PaddleOCR, Baidu,
Apache License 2.0) through rten (MIT OR Apache-2.0), a pure-Rust ONNX runtime. The models are not part of LightCraft
and are never distributed with it: a user downloads them only when they choose to, pinned by size and SHA-256.

Finding people runs YuNet (face_detection_yunet_2023mar, MIT License, Copyright (c) 2020 Shiqi Yu) and SFace
(face_recognition_sface_2021dec, Apache License 2.0, Beijing University of Posts and Telecommunications) from the OpenCV
Zoo through rten. The models are not part of LightCraft and are never distributed with it: a user downloads them only when
they choose to, pinned by size and SHA-256. LightCraft's code reads their published input and output conventions; it
contains no code from OpenCV.

AI denoise weights are not part of LightCraft and are never distributed with it.
The default build offers user-supplied models only. The optional rawnind-model
feature offers a separately downloaded RawNIND UtNet2 Bayer checkpoint under
GPL-3.0 (https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html), after the user accepts its terms.
Commercial use is subject to those terms, including applicable source, licence and
notice obligations on redistribution. Enabling that offer in releases remains a
maintainer decision. The ONNX reader and CPU/GPU executor are our Rust implementation;
no darktable, RawSpeed, LibRaw or other GPL decoder/runtime code is included.

Builds made with craft-fonts (the optional CRAFT_FONTS_DIR build input; all official releases)
also embed the fonts listed in https://github.com/storytold/craft-fonts/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md
(BIZ UDPGothic, BIZ UDMincho, Shippori Mincho, Noto Sans CJK SC, Noto Sans Arabic and Noto Sans
Thai), under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. The web build embeds BIZ UDPGothic Regular and Noto
Sans Thai Regular, and loads Noto Sans CJK SC separately. Release packages include each font's
licence as OFL-<family>.txt; Windows installers include their texts in FONT-LICENCES.txt.

Place names for reverse geocoding (Photo > Fill Location from GPS) are not part of LightCraft and
are never distributed with it. On the user's request (Photo > Download Place Names) the app
downloads cities15000.zip, admin1CodesASCII.txt and countryInfo.txt from GeoNames
(https://download.geonames.org/export/dump/) into the settings folder. GeoNames data is licensed
under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/);
attribution: "GeoNames, geonames.org". The lookup code (crates/geocode) is our own.

